Availability: SDD

Purpose:
  Define availability levels, RTO/RPO targets, and HA patterns.
  Availability is selected based on business criticality, not defaulted
  to the highest level.

Owns: architecture/availability.sdd

Principles:
  Availability MUST be selected based on business criticality.
  Higher availability requires proportional investment.
  RTO and RPO MUST be defined before architecture selection.
  Backup is NOT a substitute for high availability.
  Failover MUST be tested regularly.

AvailabilityLevels:

  L99:
    name: Standard
    downtime_year: 3.65 days
    rto: 24 hours
    rpo: 24 hours
    pattern: single instance, daily backups, manual recovery

  L99_9:
    name: Production
    downtime_year: 8.76 hours
    rto: 4 hours
    rpo: 1 hour
    pattern: multi-instance, automated backups, automated failover

  L99_95:
    name: High Availability
    downtime_year: 4.38 hours
    rto: 1 hour
    rpo: 15 minutes
    pattern: multi-zone, active-passive, near-real-time replication

  L99_99:
    name: Critical
    downtime_year: 52.56 minutes
    rto: 15 minutes
    rpo: 5 minutes
    pattern: multi-zone active-active, automated failover

  L99_999:
    name: Mission Critical
    downtime_year: 5.26 minutes
    rto: 1 minute
    rpo: seconds
    pattern: multi-region active-active, real-time replication

RTO_RPO:
  RTO: Maximum acceptable downtime (time from failure to restoration)
  RPO: Maximum acceptable data loss (time between last backup and failure)
  rule: RPO <= backup frequency, RTO >= estimated recovery time

HAPatterns:
  ActivePassive: primary handles traffic, standby takes over on failure
  ActiveActive: multiple nodes handle traffic simultaneously
  MultiZone: deploy across multiple availability zones
  MultiRegion: deploy across multiple geographic regions

BackupStrategies:
  FullBackup: complete copy, frequency based on availability level
  IncrementalBackup: changed data since last backup
  ContinuousBackup: real-time via replication (L99.99+)
  rule: backups MUST be tested by restoration at least quarterly

FailoverMechanisms:
  AutomatedFailover: automatic detection and promotion (L99.9+)
  ManualFailover: human-initiated, requires tested runbook
  GracefulDegradation: reduce functionality rather than fail completely

DisasterRecovery:
  DRPlan: documented procedure with RTO/RPO, recovery procedures, escalation
  DRTesting: frequency based on availability level (quarterly to continuous)
  DRTypes:
    backup_restore: restore from backup (L99-L99.9)
    warm_standby: scaled-down version running (L99.99)
    multi_site_active: full infrastructure in multiple regions (L99.999)

Selection:
  AI MUST select availability level based on:
    business criticality, revenue impact, data loss tolerance,
    regulatory requirements, budget, team capability

  Availability MUST NOT be selected at maximum level by default.

AntiPatterns:
  MaximumByDefault: MUST have documented business case for L99.999
  BackupAsHA: backups complement HA, they do not replace it
  UntestedFailover: MUST test failover per DRTesting frequency
  SingleRegionProduction: L99.95+ MUST have documented DR plan
  SilentDegradation: degraded mode MUST generate alerts
  NoRunbook: manual failover MUST have tested runbook

Navigation:
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd

State: +
